Today is Friday morning.
I sit near my desk in the office.
I am working on my computer.
I have written some new code.
Vikram comes near my desk.
He is our team's excellent tester.
"Maya, I have seen your code," Vikram says.
"I have found two small mistakes there," he says.
I am not sad.
Vikram's eye is sharp.
"Where are the mistakes, Vikram?" I ask.
He points on my computer.
"Here is one mistake, and there is the second," he says.
I see those two mistakes.
"Thank you, Vikram."
"You have tested it well," I say.
"I will fix these two mistakes right now," I say.
I quickly make a change in my code.
I have corrected my work quickly.
Now my code is fine.
Vikram is also satisfied.
